FixedRateIrm::onMarketPause(bool)
├── given market is unset
│   └── when owner or another address calls with either pause flag
│       ├── it should revert with IrmUnauthorized
│       ├── it should preserve the complete IRState owner and market
│       └── it should emit no events
└── given market is bound
    ├── when caller is owner or another address other than the bound market
    │   ├── it should revert with IrmUnauthorized for either pause flag
    │   ├── it should preserve the complete IRState owner and market
    │   └── it should emit no events
    └── when caller is the bound market
        ├── when paused is true
        │   └── when called repeatedly at normal and oversized timestamps
        │       ├── it should preserve the complete IRState owner and market
        │       └── it should emit no events
        └── when paused is false
            ├── when timestamp is within uint48
            │   └── it should set lastUpdate to the current timestamp
            ├── when called repeatedly at the same and later timestamps
            │   └── it should update lastUpdate and emit even when the timestamp is unchanged
            ├── when timestamp is zero or type(uint48).max
            │   └── it should accept the exact boundary timestamp
            ├── when timestamp exceeds type(uint48).max
            │   └── it should truncate to the low 48 bits rather than revert
            ├── it should preserve borrowRate owner and market
            └── it should emit exactly one IRStateUpdated with the resulting state
